Keep SBR and PS exponent shifts within the operand width.

The SBR envelope and PS energies are mantissa/exponent pairs; aligning
them shifts by exponent differences that a malformed stream drives below
0 or to 32 and more, undefined in C++ (UBSan reports):
- calc_sbr_envelope.cpp: sbr_align()/sbr_shl() clamp the shifts to
  0..31 (the arithmetic result is already 0 or -1 there), as is the
  quotient of nL/(1 + nL) computed from wrapped noise levels; the energy
  estimation of a band with ui == li no longer divides by 0, and the
  high-band energy is renormalised when bit 30 is set (aux2 == -1).
- sbr_aliasing_reduction.cpp: alias_align(), the same clamp.
- sbr_envelope_unmapping.cpp: unmap_shr() clamps the envelope and noise
  exponents of the coupled channel to 31.
- ps_pwr_transient_detection.cpp: wrapped energies gave a ratio of 1 or
  more, a negative shift; the gain saturates as in the peakDiff <= nrg
  branch.

Regression input:
tools/aacdec-fuzz/regressions/t169-sbr-envelope-shift.bin.

